    T269
        title        P06 — Implement ActorEngine and lifecycle
        status       in_progress
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T255, @T256, @T257, @T262, @T263, @T264, @T265, @T266, @T267, @T268]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.RuntimeV2.D2,
                     @plan.RuntimeV2.C2,
                     @plan.RuntimeV2.V1,
                     @plan.RuntimeV2.V4,
                     @plan.RuntimeV2.V5,
                     @plan.Verification.D2,
                     @plan.Verification.V2
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.27.6 (in progress, assigned to Arpit Bharti at
            migration); this Workflow Task is in progress.
            Deliverable: implement the single per-actor owner for state, turns,
            lifecycle, restoration, activities, and shutdown.
            Allowed paths: runtime-next actor engine/actor modules and assigned owner
            tests; keep package-root exports and frozen runtime unchanged. Existing
            uncommitted implementation changes match this scope; T266–T268 remain blockers
            to acceptance, and the source review findings remain unresolved.
        acceptance
            - One preflight and total cut covers store, evidence, actor state, context,
            and receipt; failed planning leaves no partial state or work.
            - Admission, reentrancy, observer isolation, flush races, mapped chains,
            bounded snapshots, and cleanup pass.
            - Fresh actors initialize once; restore and resume never replay input or
            initialization, and publish the exact active leaf.
            - Restoration, timers, activities, acknowledgements, suspension, streams,
            and shutdown preserve owner truth.
            - Public sends return synchronously; internal and Story acknowledgments
            settle after publication and evidence, before sinks or user work.
            - Typed failures, defects, and interruption settle each acknowledgment;
            pre-commit defects retain prior state and publish one issue-only snapshot.
            - No duplicate actor/lifecycle authority, post-commit expected failure,
            drain polling, unbounded queue, or production test hook remains.
            - This Task carries the Runtime O4 actor-turn/publication implementation;
            O4 remains pending until Operations O1 store/capture and Story O6
            acknowledgment proofs pass with their owner Tasks.
            - Every assigned scenario passes; no P06-owned placeholder remains;
            package checks/build and review gates pass.
            - Evidence: owner scenario results, lifecycle and cleanup proofs, scoped
            package checks/build, and review receipts are recorded in this Workflow Task
            handback.

