    T272
        title       Fix Implementation provider boundary
        status      done
        priority    high
        derives_from [@plan.RuntimeV2.O3]
        description
            Deliverable: keep provider identity and native Layer acquisition private to the
            Implementation owner so callers cannot mutate duplicate detection or acquire
            services outside Runtime readiness.

            Plan commitment -> Runtime O3 requires service installation only at the Runtime
            boundary and Implementation acquisition during readiness. Task acceptance -> preserve
            factory composition and inferred service/error/requirement types while making service
            identity immutable and keeping the native Layer unavailable to callers. Owner ->
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/implementation/implementation.ts. Proof -> focused
            Implementation behavior and compile-time tests; expected baseline: mutating public
            serviceKeys bypasses duplicate detection, returned implementations expose `.layer`,
            and constructor access can create provider-like objects with unchecked identity metadata.

